                <pb facs="0765" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg751"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish, Secretary of
                        State, to Mr. Roberts, Spanish minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi>
                        8, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p>The undersigned, Secretary of State of the United States, has the honor to
                    transmit to Mr. Lopez Roberts a copy of a note of the 5th instant, which he has
                    received from Mr. Freyre, the minister of Peru, conveying his assent, on behalf
                    of his government, to the departure of the gun-boats constructed for the Spanish
                    government by Mr. Delamater, of New York; also a copy of the reply thereto by
                    the undersigned.</p>
                <p>The undersigned offers to Mr. Lopez Roberts on this occasion renewed assurances
                    of his highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>HAMILTON FISH.</item>
                            <item>Señor Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Lopez
                                Roberts</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
